system "ALA-LC:bul-Cyrl:Latn:1997" {

metadata {
  authority_id alalc
  id 1997
  language iso-639-2:bul
  source_script Cyrl
  destination_script Latn
  name Romanization Table -- Bulgarian (1997)
  url http://www.rechtertie.nl/databases/judd/downloads/Bulgarian.pdf
  creation_date 1997

  notes {
    note "      The letter Ъ in the initial and medial position is a vowel in Bulgarian and is romanized as ŭ.\n      It appears in the final position chiefly in texts published before 1945, in which it serves as\n      a hard sign and is romanized as ʺ."
    note "The letters Ѣ and Ѫ are found chiefly in texts published before the orthographic reform of 1945."
  }
}

tests {
  # missing
# Exhaustive per-row tests for alalc-bul-Cyrl-Latn-1997, generated from the source
# document's table.
# Source: ALA-LC Bulgarian Romanization Table, 2013 version, p. 1 (letter
# table) + p. 2 (notes); held source
# interscript-private-references/alalc/alalc-bulgarian.pdf. Extraction: PDF
# text layer, every value cell cross-checked against the rendered page
# image. The map is the 1997 table; the only locally-held printed source is
# the 2013 version (the table page lists "Earlier versions: 2012, 2011,
# 1997"). The letter table and notes match what the map encodes, so the rows
# pin the map against the held printed page; the version difference is
# recorded here. The value cells for Ц, Ю, Я, Ѣ print the tesh-ligature
# digraphs (t͡s, i͡u, i͡a, i͡e, U+0361); the text layer stores lookalike
# Cyrillic glyphs for these — transcribed from the printed image. The upper
# Ѫ value cell is blank in the text layer and visually identified at 900 dpi
# as U̐ (U + U+0310), matching the printed lower u̐. Skipped printed rows:
# Ъ/ъ — the table gives Ъ two value cells: "Ŭ (see note 1)" (the vowel
# reading, initial/medial) and "ʺ (hard sign)" (the pre-1945 word-final
# reading). The map implements note 1 with a word-final rule, so a plain-row
# test of the standalone letter takes the word-final path; both cells are
# position-dependent per note 1 and not expressible as plain rows. Only the
# note-1 context is documented here; the Ŭ/ŭ cells were transcribed and
# failed only because the standalone string is word-final.
# Canonical-equivalence notes: Й: printed glyph "Ĭ"; the runtime emits the
# canonically equivalent byte form 'Ĭ'; the row is stored in the runtime's
# byte form so the byte-exact embedded test passes. | й: printed glyph "ĭ";
# the runtime emits the canonically equivalent byte form 'ĭ'; the row is
# stored in the runtime's byte form so the byte-exact embedded test passes.
# Provenance artifact: scripts/row-sources/alalc-bul-Cyrl-Latn-1997.json (62 rows).
# generated-by: maps/scripts/gen-row-tests.mjs (2026-11-16); regenerate from the artifact, do not hand-edit.
